nvc0's code generation through the disk cache (Mesa 20.3 added one upstream, after splitting
nv50_ir_prog_info; this is a smaller equivalent for 20.1): nvc0_program_translate looks the
translated program (code, header, relocations, fixups, header-generator state) up by a key of its
inputs (chipset, stage, TGSI tokens, user clip planes, shared memory size) before running nv50_ir.
Fixup function pointers are stored as indices into the GM107 emitter's table (the only emitter in
the Switch build; programs with other fixups are not cached). Compute and stream output programs
are not cached.

